{"assets":["/statement-assets/9725e7e97033a684b08c2cf9fff44410084fc362b4667037109192ce6d7522f7.png","/statement-assets/7767c6c3fb8164b900ac5f4404872ad15574aa982984d8b31836449c153e3a60.png","/statement-assets/84b2177e0f4f36f0f8c6f89994852fd08406c012b4be6b061acfe1a693ba76db.png","/statement-assets/b288aad2bcf2e3ec329c3498f674675bd7daf0d0bcd1cf8eeb9b0dd19aaf7467.png","/statement-assets/085f537732537683682e98069f9032545b3cc63b9679b77bb4fc3a4c8f0f6f8f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"149","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Coloring Brackets"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Once Petya read a problem about a bracket sequence. He gave it much thought but didn't find a solution. Today you will face it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":". It represents a correct bracket sequence. A correct bracket sequence is the sequence of opening (\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\") and closing (\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\") brackets, such that it is possible to obtain a correct mathematical expression from it, inserting numbers and operators between the brackets. For example, such sequences as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are correct bracket sequences and such sequences as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a correct bracket sequence each bracket corresponds to the matching bracket (an opening bracket corresponds to the matching closing bracket and vice versa). For example, in a bracket sequence shown of the figure below, the third bracket corresponds to the matching sixth one and the fifth bracket corresponds to the fourth one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/9725e7e97033a684b08c2cf9fff44410084fc362b4667037109192ce6d7522f7.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are allowed to color some brackets in the bracket sequence so as all three conditions are fulfilled: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Each bracket is either not colored any color, or is colored red, or is colored blue. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For any pair of matching brackets exactly one of them is colored. In other words, for any bracket the following is true: either it or the matching bracket that corresponds to it is colored. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" No two neighboring colored brackets have the same color. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the number of different ways to color the bracket sequence. The ways should meet the above-given conditions. Two ways of coloring are considered different if they differ in the color of at least one bracket. As the result can be quite large, print it modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains the single string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ |s| ≤ 700"},{"kind":"text","text":") which represents a correct bracket sequence. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the only number — the number of ways to color the bracket sequence that meet the above given conditions modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"(())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"(()())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"40\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"()\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the first sample test. The bracket sequence from the sample can be colored, for example, as is shown on two figures below. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/7767c6c3fb8164b900ac5f4404872ad15574aa982984d8b31836449c153e3a60.png"},"kind":"image"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/84b2177e0f4f36f0f8c6f89994852fd08406c012b4be6b061acfe1a693ba76db.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The two ways of coloring shown below are incorrect. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b288aad2bcf2e3ec329c3498f674675bd7daf0d0bcd1cf8eeb9b0dd19aaf7467.png"},"kind":"image"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/085f537732537683682e98069f9032545b3cc63b9679b77bb4fc3a4c8f0f6f8f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"149D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/149/problem/D"}